<title>ISRAEL: Shekel fix little changed after heavy intervention.</title>
<headline>Shekel fix little changed after heavy intervention.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The shekel representative rate was fixed almost unchanged against the dollar and a key basket of foreign currencies on Tuesday after the Bank of Israel intervened heavily, dealers said.</p>
<p>They estimated the central bank bought close to $500 million, including dollar purchases, since it set Monday's representative rate.</p>
</text>
